"""Q40: write Q40 result into /output/report.json (idempotent). usage: python3 -I s234_update_report_q40.py"""
import json
R=json.load(open('/output/report.json')); R['results']=[x for x in R['results'] if not str(x.get('quantity','')).startswith('Q40')]
EV=('/workspace/scripts/s230_q40_isotopologue_fit.py, s231_q40_summary.py, s232_q40_residuals.py, s233_q40_lowX.py -> out/q40/summary.txt, summary.json, residuals.txt, fit.log, lowX.log (builds on s220a/b Q39 grid)')
ASM=[dict(name='data',value='Harada+2018 Table 13 1.7" peak pixel: H13CO+ 1-0 and 3-2 at N (9.4+-0.95, 2.6+-0.49 K km/s; HCO+ 205.3, 91.6) and H13CO+ 1-0 at C (3.44+-0.95); S not tabulated. H13CN is not in Harada Table 13 and H13CN 3-2 (259.0 GHz) falls in the gap between Xb4f windows; Xb47 H13CN 4-3 is blended with the CO 3-2 wing (Q4/Q16 limits HCN/H13CN>8-9) and is far weaker than the 1-0 data, so not used. H13CN 1-0 and S H13CO+ come from our short-spacing-complete 2.2" maps (Q29, s185): N H13CN/HCN peak pixel 0.030+-0.006; S H13CO+/HCO+ 0.014+-0.009 (peak), S H13CN/HCN 0.0057+-0.0059; C (Bridge) H13CN/HCN 0.0237+-0.0044 (aperture), applied to the Harada 12C intensities (1.7" vs 2.2" beam mismatch: variant A, flagged).'),
     dict(name='model',value='Q39 one-gas RADEX fine grid (HCN, HCO+, CS; Tk 10-300 K, log n 3-8, columns on 0.05 dex); 13C species at the same Tk, n, filling and band scale with column N/X, X = 12C/13C = 25, 30, 40, 60, 90 (assumed, not measured for NGC 3256; shift rounded to 0.05 dex); LAMDA HCO+/HCN files used for the 13C lines (no frequency/A scaling, ~10% in sigma). Isotopologue data in linear K km/s with sigma^2 = err^2 + (10% obs)^2 + (10% model)^2. Variants: H = Harada H13CO+ only (matched beam, cleanest); A = H + Q29 H13CN/S/C data; B = Q29 2.2" aperture ratios for all.'),
     dict(name='limits',value='Single-zone model: the thick N core and the thin envelope are not separated. Tk saturates at the 300 K cap. chi2 differences are indicative (non-Gaussian, 8-9 data, 6 parameters).')]
R['results'].append(dict(quantity='Q40: can the 13C isotopologue data (H13CO+ 1-0/3-2, H13CN 1-0) exclude the cold/dense optically thick branch of the N one-gas RADEX posterior? Effect on N(HCN)/N(HCO+) and the N/S contrast',
 target='N, S, Bridge(C); 1.7" peak pixel (Harada) with Q29 2.2" supplements',
 value=('YES for 12C/13C <~60, NO (and the one-zone model fails) for 90. Without 13C (Q39): the cold/dense branch (Tk~11-30 K, log n 5.5-7, tau(HCO+ 1-0) >>1) is 4.5 chi2 above the hot branch (P(Tk<=30 K)=0.72 in the posterior). '
        'Adding the matched-beam Harada H13CO+ 1-0 and 3-2 at N (R(1-0)=HCO+/H13CO+=21.8, R(3-2)=35, K km/s 3-2/1-0 of H13CO+ = 0.28+-0.06): dchi2(best Tk<=30 K - best hot) = 32 (X=25), 27 (X=30), 17 (X=40), 5.2 (X=60), -1.3 (X=90; posterior P(Tk<=30)=0.00/0.00/0.00/0.02/0.58). With H13CN 1-0 too (variant A): 41/38/28/10/0.2; with 2.2" aperture ratios (variant B, X=40/60/90): 23/18/7. '
        'The discriminator is the H13CO+ 3-2/1-0 ratio: the cold/dense branch predicts 0.4-0.7 where 0.28+-0.06 is observed; the hot branch predicts 0.25-0.35. At X=90 the N fit with 13C data is itself poor (best chi2 17-23 for 8-9 data, vs 4.6 without) i.e. X>~70 with a one-zone model is disfavoured by the data, not the branch distinction. The N fit prefers X ~30-40 (chi2 5.3 at X=30, 7.0 at X=40, 12.7 at X=60 with Harada alone), lower than the usual 40-90 assumed range, or equivalently some of the HCO+ 1-0 is optically thicker/ more extended than the single zone. '
        'Consequences when the cold branch is removed (X<=60): the N posterior is hot (Tk 170-300 K, at the cap, log n 4.6-4.8), N(HCN)/N(HCO+) at N = 3.5 [3.1,3.8] (X=40), 3.8 [3.3,4.7] (X=60) vs S 2.2 [1.9,2.6] and C 2.3 [2.1,2.6]; N/S contrast 1.6 [1.3,1.9] (X=40, P(>1)=0.99, profile 2.1 sigma), 1.76 [1.4,2.3] (X=60, 2.1 sigma), 1.6 (X=25/30, 2.1-2.2 sigma); S and C are unconstrained by the Harada isotopologues (H13CO+ not tabulated at S). The marginal P(>1) goes 0.52 (Q39 fine grid, bimodal) -> 0.99, but the PROFILE significance stays 2.1 sigma, because the excess is limited by the S/N of the 12C lines, not by the thick branch. '
        'Adding our 2.2" S/C isotopologue data (variant A) raises N/S to 2.8 (X=60) - 4.4 sigma (X=25) but makes S fit badly (S chi2 12-45 for X<=60: S H13CO+/HCO+ and the H13CN limit want X>~90) so these are not adopted; N and S cannot share one 12C/13C with these data unless opacity differs. Bridge/S stays 1.0-1.1 (0.4-0.9 sigma). '
        'CONCLUSION: the optically thick cold branch is excluded (dchi2>=17 for X<=40, >=5 for X=60) with the 1.7" H13CO+ pair; N(HCN)/N(HCO+) at N ~3.5 (+-0.4) and N/S 1.6-1.8 survive at 2.1 sigma (profile); the abundance excess is NOT upgraded to >3 sigma.'),
 unit='chi2; dimensionless; K; cm-3',uncertainty='X=12C/13C assumed (25-90); chi2 differences from a 8-9 point non-Gaussian likelihood; profile intervals dchi2<1; peak-pixel 1.7" Harada vs 2.2" Q29 beams not identical (10% sigma added)',
 method='Q39 fine-grid RADEX + 13C isotopologue lines at fixed 12C/13C (s230-s233)',evidence=EV,confidence='low',assumptions=ASM))
json.dump(R,open('/output/report.json','w'),indent=1)
